WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.540
Knitting in fairisle or two colors across

2
00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:07.940
each row is a staple
technique for machine knitters.

3
00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.170
Placing yarn in each yarn feeder

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.580
of the carriage and setting
the machine correctly.

5
00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.380
You can knit stranded knitting

6
00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:19.700
in a fraction of the time
as knitting it by hand.

7
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:24.600
Start by knitting a few
rows in plain knitting

8
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.460
end with the carriage on the left.

9
00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:30.940
Lock the card on the first row.

10
00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:35.460
By setting the card lock
lever to the circle.

11
00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:41.820
Engage the patterning device
by setting the change knob to KC

12
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:46.000
and knit from left to right.

13
00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:56.340
Notice that there are needles in working
position B and middle position D.

14
00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:03.060
Press the upper MC button to tell the
carriage you want to knit in Fairisle.

15
00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:07.290
Release the card lock
lever with the triangle.

16
00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:12.700
This will allow the punch card to advance.

17
00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:17.540
Thread the second yarn in the mast
and position it in the B feeder.

18
00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.540
Now you don't need to open the gate.

19
00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:26.620
Just snap the yarn into place, wiggle it
around to make sure it flows smoothly.

20
00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:32.760
Hold that new yarn with your
left hand and begin knitting.

21
00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:42.210
Notice that the yarns are being carried
across the back of the knitting.

22
00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.180
As you pass the carriage,

23
00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:48.340
following the punch card,
needles are being selected for the next

24
00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:55.600
row, and both colors are being
knit in turn across the row.

25
00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:12.920
As you pass the carriage, the punch card
automatically advances to the next row.

26
00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.860
This pattern repeats every two rows,

27
00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:25.480
alternating the colors
according to the punch card.

